  "assumptions": [
    {
      "id": "A-env",
      "text": "Environment terms (the state before the action, the results of opaque calls) are free: every value of them is possible. The result of an opaque call is a function of its function and arguments."
    },
    {
      "id": "A-implicit",
      "text": "Implicit Go panics other than an integer division by zero (nil dereference, index out of range, a nil map write, a failed type assertion) are not modelled as guards."
    },
    {
      "id": "A-kv",
      "text": "A KV store maps key bytes to value bytes; Get of an absent key is the empty value, Has(k) is Get(k) != empty (a stored value is never empty), Delete writes the empty value. A KV call's error result is free; a Set or Delete that returns an error is modelled as having written."
    },
    {
      "id": "A-loop",
      "text": "A loop is not iterated: every family it may write is havocked and its values are unknown after it."
    },
    {
      "id": "A-reach",
      "text": "Every path that returns a non-nil error or panics before writing is a guard reach."
    },
    {
      "id": "A-reentrancy",
      "text": "An opaque call writes only state reachable from its arguments (and its receiver): a state pointer, map, KV store or closure handed to it havocs the families it reaches; a call through an interface held in the state does not write this machine's state otherwise."
    }
  ],
